.TH BBFSCHECK 1
.SH NAME
bbfscheck \- filesystem health checking tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bbfscheck
\-\-summary PATH
.br
.B bbfscheck
\-\-inode PATH
.br
.B bbfscheck
\-\-scan PATH [\-\-max-depth N] [\-\-small-file BYTES]
.SH DESCRIPTION
bbfscheck reports filesystem usage, inode usage, and directory scan statistics.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-summary PATH
Show filesystem block usage for PATH.
.TP
.B \-\-inode PATH
Show inode usage for PATH.
.TP
.B \-\-scan PATH
Scan directory metadata under PATH.
.TP
.B \-\-max-depth N
Limit scan recursion depth. A depth of 0 scans only PATH itself.
.TP
.B \-\-small-file BYTES
Count regular files whose size is less than or equal to BYTES. The default is 4096.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show help text.
.SH EXAMPLES
.B bbfscheck \-\-summary /
.br
.B bbfscheck \-\-inode /
.br
.B bbfscheck \-\-scan ./testdir \-\-max-depth 3
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 for invalid arguments, 3 when system data cannot be read.
